I retain the previously-validated xmv_1, xmeas_2 (inflow) and xmv_10 (outflow) terms unchanged, since they have passed every sign check to date and represent the most robust structure found so far. I continue to exclude xmeas_21/xmeas_22 (demonstrated CW-loop control-echo confounding per Gen-1's failure), xmeas_40 (composition-analyzer sampling artifact several units downstream), and the forbidden xmv_3/xmeas_1 (lagging reactive variables per CCF test). If xmv_2's sign fails or fitness does not improve over Gen-2's 0.9263, this would reinforce that the two-term D-feed inflow + one-term CW outflow structure already captures the dominant physical signal for this target, and Gen-2 should be treated as the final, most robust answer, with no further additive elaboration warranted beyond this point.
